},"legal_source_commitment_resolved":false,"status":"INCOMPARABLE_FACT_BINDINGS"},"right_node_id":"node.bc55be7e973a689d07f9e64b"}],"failures":[{"action_id":"action.6328133ce3604958bd87452bae2003dd","details":"{'model': 'Generation', 'total_errors': 12, 'validation_errors': [{'type': 'missing', 'loc': ['readings'], 'msg': 'Field required'}, {'type': 'list_type', 'loc': ['dimensions'], 'msg': 'Input should be a valid list'}, {'type': 'missing', 'loc': ['coverage'], 'msg': 'Field required'}, {'type': 'missing', 'loc': ['questions'], 'msg': 'Field required'}, {'type': 'extra_forbidden', 'loc': ['protocol'], 'msg': 'Extra inputs are not permitted'}, {'type': 'extra_forbidden', 'loc': ['task'], 'msg': 'Extra inputs are not permitted'}, {'type': 'extra_forbidden', 'loc': ['source_key'], 'msg': 'Extra inputs are not permitted'}, {'type': 'extra_forbidden', 'loc': ['proposal_status'], 'msg': 'Extra inputs are not permitted'}, {'type': 'extra_forbidden', 'loc': ['selected_control'], 'msg': 'Extra inputs are not permitted'}, {'type': 'extra_forbidden', 'loc': ['interpretations'], 'msg': 'Extra inputs are not permitted'}, {'type': 'extra_forbidden', 'loc': ['alternative_reading_assessment'], 'msg': 'Ex","error":"E_SCHEMA","repair":"VALIDATED_OUTPUT_ONLY_MEANING_UNRESOLVED","repaired_response_hash":"b43909d4668db18659f1f0cd9ed29490d8f282b855c4777149d027cd84288371","stage":"GENERATE"}],"frontier":[],"initial":{"alternatives":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Defines distributors and the circular’s fund-distribution context.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u0.2"},{"reason":"Background heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u1.497"},{"reason":"Describes distributor-added features; does not itself classify them as gifts.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u2.512"},{"reason":"Describes investment mandates relevant to separate marketing provisions.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u3.792"},{"reason":"Marketing background; public advertising is not stated as a prerequisite for the selected gift restriction.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u4.1115"},{"reason":"Guaranteed-returns heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u5.1267"},{"reason":"Identifies the separate statutory provision.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u6.1287"},{"reason":"Distinguishes actual fund return from distributor top-up return, supporting separate identification of benefits.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u7.1360"},{"reason":"Structured-product classification remains a separate, qualified inquiry.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u8.1651"},{"reason":"Section 103 authorisation and exemption conditions belong to a separate control.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u9.1940"},{"reason":"Explains potential confusion between distributor guarantees and fund features.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u10.2239"},{"reason":"Identifies the provision governing the selected control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u11.2603"},{"reason":"Preserves qualified gift classification and applicability even without structured-product status.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"reason":"Supplies the gift restriction, product-type scope, discount exception and stated purpose.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"reason":"Connects the two controls without making every additional return automatically a breach.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u14.3675"},{"reason":"Heading for a separate subject.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u15.4022"},{"reason":"Background to redemption restrictions outside the selected control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u16.4063"},{"reason":"Separate fairness and redemption requirements.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u17.4359"},{"reason":"Separate dealing-frequency expectations and administrative qualifications.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u18.4879"},{"reason":"Heading for separate marketing requirements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u19.5230"},{"reason":"Separate misleading-information control under paragraph 2.3.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u20.5257"},{"reason":"Separate advertising-guidelines dependency.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u21.5903"},{"reason":"Separate restrictions on risk and deposit-like representations.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u22.6374"},{"reason":"Monitoring and potential future action do not add a condition to the selected restriction.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u23.7007"},{"reason":"Departmental attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u24.7186"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u25.7275"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u26.7393"},{"reason":"Offering-document footnote supports disclosure context, not the discount exception.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u27.7511"},{"reason":"Identifies the Code of Conduct referenced by the selected restriction.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u28.7987"},{"reason":"Identifies supporting FAQ and its issue date; its answer is not supplied.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u29.8110"},{"reason":"Supplementation language concerns advertising guidelines, not an express amendment of the gift restriction.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u30.8235"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The stated actors are distributors. Promotion to a client covers both specific products and particular product types, including certain fund types and fund houses. The selected application remains within the circular’s SFC-authorised-fund context.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Neither gift nor discount is exhaustively defined. Additional returns and incentives may be gifts; that classification is not automatic. Actual fund return and distributor top-up return are expressly distinguished.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u7.1360","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The parenthetical exception attaches to discounts of fees or charges. A separately identifiable discount does not expressly exempt another benefit in a combined offer. Whether a fee-linked rebate actually qualifies as a discount remains unresolved.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The selected standard says should not offer. The proposed compliance predicate models conformity to that stated standard without converting it into the separate statutory offence. May be considered preserves judgment over classification.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u9.1940","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The restriction concerns offering gifts during promotion. No effective date, transition period or payment deadline is supplied. The FAQ’s 30 September 2010 date identifies a source, not a commencement date.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987","db43e253bea18.u29.8110"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The gift control is independently relevant even when an arrangement is not a structured product. The Code and supporting FAQ are identified but not supplied in full; section 103 authorisation or exemption does not establish satisfaction of the gift control.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u9.1940","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u14.3675","db43e253bea18.u28.7987","db43e253bea18.u29.8110"],"status":"PROPOSED"}],"questions":["What distinguishes a genuine discount of fees or charges from a cash incentive calculated by reference to fees, particularly where payment is conditional on continued investment?","What criteria in the referenced Code and FAQ determine gift classification and linkage to a particular product type?","For a combined offer, which benefits are independently identifiable, and which form a single economically inseparable benefit?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The selected control assesses one identified benefit offered by one distributor in the SFC-authorised-fund context.","Separately identifiable benefits in a combined offer are assessed separately; identifying those benefits may require judgment.","Gift classification, discount classification and promotional linkage are supplied judgments, not inferred from a benefit’s label or from the mere existence of additional returns.","The result is interpreted only when scope is true; unknown facts remain unknown."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u0.2"},{"quote":"(i) the actual return of the relevant fund(s) invested by the investor (ie, fund return); and (ii) a top-up return to make up the difference between the fund return and the guaranteed rate of return offered by the distributor.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u7.1360"},{"quote":"Even where the guaranteed returns offered would not constitute a “structured product” under the SFO","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u14.3675"}],"distinction":"The discount exception applies to the identified benefit, while product-type promotion remains covered. For example, an offer promoting funds of one fund house could combine a fee reduction with a separately identifiable shopping voucher. Assuming the voucher is a gift and not a fee discount, the fee reduction satisfies this control and the voucher fails it. The text does not support exempting the entire package because one component is a discount, or excluding it because no individual fund is singled out. A fee-linked cash rebate presents a genuine unresolved classification question: if it is a discount it satisfies this control; if it is a non-discount gift it fails. The packet does not supply enough criteria to choose between those classifications.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The offeror is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds in the transaction being assessed.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit is offered to a client in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product, including a relevant fund type or funds offered by a particular fund house.","name":"benefit_has_product_promotion_link","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit qualifies as a gift under the referenced paragraph 3.11 standard; being an additional return or incentive alone does not establish this fact.","name":"benefit_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit itself qualifies as a discount of fees or charges, rather than merely accompanying a separate discount.","name":"benefit_is_fee_or_charge_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(or (not benefit_is_gift) benefit_is_fee_or_charge_discount)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor benefit_has_product_promotion_link)"},"local_id":"gift_component_control","questions":["Does the identified benefit qualify as a gift, and if so does it itself constitute a discount of fees or charges?","Does the referenced FAQ clarify treatment of rebates or inseparable combined benefits?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] For the selected control, Paragraph 3.11 gift restriction for one offered benefit, true means that the in-scope benefit is either not a gift or qualifies for the fee-or-charge discount exception. False means that it is an in-scope gift outside that exception and fails the stated should-not-offer standard. This is a proposed interpretation of that control only; it does not determine compliance of other offer components, section 103 compliance or whole-firm compliance.","subject":"A separately identified benefit offered by a distributor during promotion to a client"}]},"controlled-language":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Defines distributors and the circular’s fund-distribution context.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u0.2"},{"reason":"Background heading only.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u1.497"},{"reason":"Explains distributor-added features; does not establish that every additional feature is a gift.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u2.512"},{"reason":"Describes investment mandates relevant to separate marketing controls.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u3.792"},{"reason":"Describes marketing practices without limiting the gift restriction to public campaigns.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u4.1115"},{"reason":"Topic heading only.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u5.1267"},{"reason":"Identifies the separate statutory advertising control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u6.1287"},{"reason":"Distinguishes underlying fund return from distributor top-up return; supports separate classification of components.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u7.1360"},{"reason":"Conditional structured-product classification belongs to a separate control.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u8.1651"},{"reason":"Section 103 offence and its authorisation or exemption conditions are outside the selected gift control.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u9.1940"},{"reason":"Misleading-impression concerns provide context; offering-document obligations are separate.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u10.2239"},{"reason":"Identifies the Code provision governing the selected control.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u11.2603"},{"reason":"Preserves conditional gift classification and independence from structured-product status.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"reason":"States the gift restriction, discount exception and product-type linkage.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"reason":"Confirms the distinct statutory and Code grounds; additional returns are restricted when in breach of either provision.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u14.3675"},{"reason":"Separate dealing-frequency topic heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u15.4022"},{"reason":"Background to redemption restrictions, outside the selected control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u16.4063"},{"reason":"Fairness and redemption-right requirements are separate controls.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u17.4359"},{"reason":"Dealing-frequency and best-endeavours requirements are separate controls.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u18.4879"},{"reason":"Separate marketing topic heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u19.5230"},{"reason":"Misleading-information requirements for service advertising are separate controls.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u20.5257"},{"reason":"Advertising Guidelines consistency requirement is outside the selected control.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u21.5903"},{"reason":"Risk and deposit-comparison advertising restrictions are separate controls.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u22.6374"},{"reason":"Monitoring and possible regulatory action do not supply a gift-classification rule or commencement date.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u23.7007"},{"reason":"Organisational attribution only.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u24.7186"},{"reason":"Organisational attribution only.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u25.7275"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution only.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u26.7393"},{"reason":"Offering-document disclosure footnote concerns a separate obligation.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u27.7511"},{"reason":"Supplies the full title of the referenced Code.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u28.7987"},{"reason":"Identifies dated FAQ support for product-type linkage; the FAQ answer itself is absent.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u29.8110"},{"reason":"Supplementary advertising guidance concerns the separate advertising control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u30.8235"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The selected application concerns distributors promoting SFC-authorised funds to clients, including a specific product or a particular product type. Public advertising, online distribution and an actual investment are not stated prerequisites. The quoted Code wording may extend beyond funds, but that broader application is outside this selected application.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Distributors are identified, but gift and discount are not exhaustively defined. Guaranteed returns and other incentives may be gifts; their status is not automatic. Fund returns and distributor top-ups are distinct components.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2","db43e253bea18.u7.1360","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The fee-or-charge discount exception attaches to the benefit classified as a discount. Its presence in a combined offer does not expressly exempt another gift component. Whether a rebate or top-up qualifies as a discount requires classification.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The operative wording is 'should not offer'; 'may be considered a gift' qualifies classification, not permission to offer a benefit already classified as a non-exempt gift. The proposed prohibition label represents this selected Code restriction, not a finding of a statutory offence.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987","db43e253bea18.u14.3675"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The control concerns offering gifts during promotion and specifies no duration, threshold or commencement date. The 30 September 2010 date identifies referenced FAQ material, not an effective date established by this packet.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987","db43e253bea18.u29.8110"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"Gift assessment remains relevant when an arrangement is not a structured product. Section 103 authorisation or exemption is not stated to disapply paragraph 3.11. The full Code and referenced FAQ answer are not supplied, limiting resolution of classification questions.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u9.1940","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u14.3675","db43e253bea18.u28.7987","db43e253bea18.u29.8110"],"status":"PROPOSED"}],"questions":["What criteria distinguish a gift from an underlying fund return, distributor top-up or other incentive in the particular arrangement?","Does the particular rebate or return reduce identifiable fees or charges, and which component qualifies for the discount exception?","What does the referenced FAQ answer say about product-type linkage and combined offers?","What applicable Code version and commencement provisions govern the assessed offer? Neither is established by this packet."],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The selected control is applied to one separately identified benefit component offered by one distributor to a client in a fund promotion.","Each component of a combined offer is assessed separately; a discount component does not transfer its exception to another component.","Gift status and discount status are supplied as reasoned classifications, not inferred solely from the label 'guaranteed return' or 'incentive'.","A product-type link is sufficient without naming one fund; actual investor distraction is not an additional prerequisite.","The formalization addresses the selected gift restriction only. It does not decide section 103 liability or overall compliance."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u0.2"},{"quote":"(i) the actual return of the relevant fund(s) invested by the investor (ie, fund return); and (ii) a top-up return to make up the difference between the fund return and the guaranteed rate of return offered by the distributor.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u7.1360"},{"quote":"Even where the guaranteed returns offered would not constitute a “structured product” under the SFO","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u14.3675"}],"distinction":"This component-level reading preserves both the product-type reach and the narrow discount exception. A combined offer can contain an exempt discount and a separately restricted gift. It also preserves the classification qualification: an additional return is not automatically a gift. The strongest uncertainty is classification of economically mixed rebates or top-ups; the supplied text does not support a definite competing classification rule.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds in the assessed arrangement.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit component is offered to a client in promoting a specific SFC-authorised fund or a particular type of such investment product, including a qualifying link to fund types or funds offered by certain fund houses.","name":"component_offered_in_linked_promotion","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The separately assessed benefit component qualifies as a gift under the selected paragraph 3.11 control; additional-return or incentive status alone does not determine this fact.","name":"component_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u7.1360","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The same assessed benefit component qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within the stated exception, irrespective of whether another component qualifies.","name":"component_is_fee_or_charge_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(and is_distributor component_offered_in_linked_promotion component_is_gift (not component_is_fee_or_charge_discount))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor component_offered_in_linked_promotion)"},"local_id":"gift_component_restriction","questions":["Can the combined benefit be separated into identifiable discount and other incentive components, or does its economic substance require a single classification?","Which evidence establishes gift status and discount status for each component?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED] For the selected paragraph 3.11 gift control, true means the assessed distributor offers this component to a client in a qualifying product or product-type promotion, the component is a gift, and it is not a discount of fees or charges. False means this component does not meet that selected restriction predicate; it does not establish overall compliance or exempt other components. Unknown classifications remain unknown. Apply the predicate separately to each component of a combined offer.","subject":"Paragraph 3.11 gift restriction applied to an individual benefit component"}]},"normative":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Defines distributors and the SFC-authorised-fund context.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u0.2"},{"reason":"Background heading only.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u1.497"},{"reason":"Describes distributor-added features without automatically classifying them as gifts.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u2.512"},{"reason":"Describes services without guaranteed rates; relevant to separate advertising controls.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u3.792"},{"reason":"Marketing observations do not make public or aggressive promotion a pre