uirement; administrative procedures do not supply a gift exception.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u18.4879"},{"reason":"Heading for other marketing controls.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u19.5230"},{"reason":"Separate misleading-advertising and paragraph 2.3 requirements.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u20.5257"},{"reason":"Separate advertising-guidelines dependency, not a condition of the gift restriction.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u21.5903"},{"reason":"Separate return-presentation and deposit-comparison restrictions.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u22.6374"},{"reason":"Monitoring and possible further action do not establish a violation or commencement date.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u23.7007"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution only.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u24.7186"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution only.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u25.7275"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution only; does not establish currency.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u26.7393"},{"reason":"Footnote supports separate offering-document disclosure requirements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u27.7511"},{"reason":"Identifies the Code's full title without determining a selected actor's licence status.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u28.7987"},{"reason":"Identifies a dated FAQ dependency; the full answer is absent.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u29.8110"},{"reason":"Identifies changing supplements to advertising guidance, not a fixed effective date.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u30.8235"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The selected control concerns intermediaries distributing SFC-authorised funds and promotion to a client of a specific product or particular product type. Section 103's person issuing an invitation to the Hong Kong public has a distinct scope.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2","db43e253bea18.u9.1940","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Actual fund return and distributor top-up are distinguished, but gift, discount and economically inseparable combined benefits lack complete classification tests. Guaranteed returns may constitute structured products or gifts; neither classification is automatic.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u7.1360","db43e253bea18.u8.1651","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The fee-or-charge discount exception modifies gifts. A qualifying discount does not itself exempt a distinct gift in the same offer. Authorisation and exemption in section 103 attach separately to that offence description.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u9.1940","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The selected rule says should not offer; gift classification says may be considered. These are preserved without converting the selected control into a statutory offence or treating all incentives as gifts. Other passages separately describe an offence, mandatory advertising compliance and possible regulatory action.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u9.1940","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987","db43e253bea18.u20.5257","db43e253bea18.u23.7007"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"2010-09-30 dates the referenced FAQ, not commencement of the selected rule. The circular date, operative Code version and transition provisions are absent. No date condition is inferred.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u29.8110","db43e253bea18.u30.8235"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The text invokes section 103, paragraph 3.11 and a FAQ despite an empty packet dependency list. Their full contents and applicable versions are unavailable. Even where makes the gift issue independently relevant when structured-product status is absent; it does not restrict the gift rule exclusively to that situation. Disclosure and advertising dependencies concern separate controls.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u6.1287","db43e253bea18.u11.2603","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u14.3675","db43e253bea18.u21.5903","db43e253bea18.u27.7511","db43e253bea18.u28.7987","db43e253bea18.u29.8110","db43e253bea18.u30.8235"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["When does a cash rebate or distributor top-up substantively qualify as a discount of fees or charges?","How should an economically inseparable combined benefit be classified or divided?","What evidence establishes linkage between a broad promotional campaign and a particular product type?","How does the quoted Code provision apply beyond the circular's SFC-authorised-fund distributor context?","What do the full FAQ and applicable Code version add, and what dates govern their application?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The evaluation unit is one selected promotional offer by one selected actor, with separately identifiable benefits assessed individually.","Component-specific treatment is an inference from the exception modifying gifts; the source supplies no allocation method for inseparable benefits.","The circular's definition of distributor supplies the actor boundary for this selected control.","Unknown classifications remain unknown; no fact values are supplied.","This is a proposal for review, not an approval or determination of legal correctness."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u0.2"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"Even where the guaranteed returns offered would not constitute a “structured product” under the SFO","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"quote":"in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u14.3675"}],"distinction":"This reading includes product-type campaigns without a named individual fund and assesses distinct gift components despite a fee discount elsewhere in the offer. It preserves the qualified classification of guaranteed returns and the independent section 103 path. The source supports unresolved classification questions more strongly than a second materially different rule: a named-product-only restriction, a blanket combined-offer exemption, automatic gift classification, or a non-structured-product prerequisite would each discard express wording. The strongest uncertainty concerns gift-versus-discount classification and inseparable benefits.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"Whether the selected actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds within the circular's definition of distributor.","name":"actor_is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Whether the selected offer is made in promotional activity directed to a client; a public invitation is not required by this fact.","name":"promotion_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Whether the selected offer promotes a specific investment product or is linked to a particular product type, including certain fund types or funds offered by certain fund houses.","name":"product_or_type_link","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Whether at least one actually offered, separately identifiable benefit component is classified as a gift and is not itself a discount of fees or charges. A discount component does not erase a distinct non-discount gift. Guaranteed returns are not automatically gifts. False requires sufficient evidence that no offered component meets both conditions; unresolved classification remains unknown.","name":"has_offered_non_discount_gift_component","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(and actor_is_distributor promotion_to_client product_or_type_link has_offered_non_discount_gift_component)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and actor_is_distributor promotion_to_client product_or_type_link)"},"local_id":"component_specific_gift_restriction","questions":["What classification evidence distinguishes a gift from a discount of fees or charges?","Can the selected combined benefit be separated substantively, and if not, how should it be classified?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED] For the selected paragraph 10 gift control, true means the selected offer is within the distributor, client and product-or-type promotional scope and includes an offered gift component that is not a discount of fees or charges, so it is caught by the quoted should-not-offer restriction. False means at least one necessary condition is established to be absent; it does not establish whole-firm compliance, licence possession or satisfaction of section 103 or other controls. The marker preserves the quoted modality and does not characterize this control as a statutory offence. A guaranteed return or incentive requires classification before the result can be determined.","subject":"Paragraph 10 gift restriction for one selected promotional offer"}]}},"java_checks":