s.","The circular's definition of distributor supplies the actor boundary for this selected control.","Unknown classifications remain unknown; no fact values are supplied.","This is a proposal for review, not an approval or determination of legal correctness."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u0.2"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"Even where the guaranteed returns offered would not constitute a “structured product” under the SFO","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"quote":"in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u14.3675"}],"distinction":"This reading includes product-type campaigns without a named individual fund and assesses distinct gift components despite a fee discount elsewhere in the offer. It preserves the qualified classification of guaranteed returns and the independent section 103 path. The source supports unresolved classification questions more strongly than a second materially different rule: a named-product-only restriction, a blanket combined-offer exemption, automatic gift classification, or a non-structured-product prerequisite would each discard express wording. The strongest uncertainty concerns gift-versus-discount classification and inseparable benefits.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"Whether the selected actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds within the circular's definition of distributor.","name":"actor_is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Whether the selected offer is made in promotional activity directed to a client; a public invitation is not required by this fact.","name":"promotion_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Whether the selected offer promotes a specific investment product or is linked to a particular product type, including certain fund types or funds offered by certain fund houses.","name":"product_or_type_link","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Whether at least one actually offered, separately identifiable benefit component is classified as a gift and is not itself a discount of fees or charges. A discount component does not erase a distinct non-discount gift. Guaranteed returns are not automatically gifts. False requires sufficient evidence that no offered component meets both conditions; unresolved classification remains unknown.","name":"has_offered_non_discount_gift_component","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(and actor_is_distributor promotion_to_client product_or_type_link has_offered_non_discount_gift_component)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and actor_is_distributor promotion_to_client product_or_type_link)"},"local_id":"component_specific_gift_restriction","questions":["What classification evidence distinguishes a gift from a discount of fees or charges?","Can the selected combined benefit be separated substantively, and if not, how should it be classified?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED] For the selected paragraph 10 gift control, true means the selected offer is within the distributor, client and product-or-type promotional scope and includes an offered gift component that is not a discount of fees or charges, so it is caught by the quoted should-not-offer restriction. False means at least one necessary condition is established to be absent; it does not establish whole-firm compliance, licence possession or satisfaction of section 103 or other controls. The marker preserves the quoted modality and does not characterize this control as a statutory offence. A guaranteed return or incentive requires classification before the result can be determined.","subject":"Paragraph 10 gift restriction for one selected promotional offer"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.968dbccb08282a4e8a580ae5","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"71639cc8d17c13c19f94db48b604f97f826619f66aec7c1c70509218f76cd211","candidate_id":"candidate.3f4062f3c2a34e3dbdf1f8fa52c3c41d","commitment":"97af37a2579f59b0ee43211f0dda2ca02feadc34272d8c9e68e6b8947e226f46","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.97af37a2579f59b0ee43211f","order":1,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["The selected control is applied to one separately identified benefit component offered by one distributor to a client in a fund promotion.","Each component of a combined offer is assessed separately; a discount component does not transfer its exception to another component.","Gift status and discount status are supplied as reasoned classifications, not inferred solely from the label 'guaranteed return' or 'incentive'.","A product-type link is sufficient without naming one fund; actual investor distraction is not an additional prerequisite.","The formalization addresses the selected gift restriction only. It does not decide section 103 liability or overall compliance."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u0.2"},{"quote":"(i) the actual return of the relevant fund(s) invested by the investor (ie, fund return); and (ii) a top-up return to make up the difference between the fund return and the guaranteed rate of return offered by the distributor.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u7.1360"},{"quote":"Even where the guaranteed returns offered would not constitute a “structured product” under the SFO","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u14.3675"}],"distinction":"This component-level reading preserves both the product-type reach and the narrow discount exception. A combined offer can contain an exempt discount and a separately restricted gift. It also preserves the classification qualification: an additional return is not automatically a gift. The strongest uncertainty is classification of economically mixed rebates or top-ups; the supplied text does not support a definite competing classification rule.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds in the assessed arrangement.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit component is offered to a client in promoting a specific SFC-authorised fund or a particular type of such investment product, including a qualifying link to fund types or funds offered by certain fund houses.","name":"component_offered_in_linked_promotion","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The separately assessed benefit component qualifies as a gift under the selected paragraph 3.11 control; additional-return or incentive status alone does not determine this fact.","name":"component_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u7.1360","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The same assessed benefit component qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within the stated exception, irrespective of whether another component qualifies.","name":"component_is_fee_or_charge_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(and is_distributor component_offered_in_linked_promotion component_is_gift (not component_is_fee_or_charge_discount))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor component_offered_in_linked_promotion)"},"local_id":"gift_component_restriction","questions":["Can the combined benefit be separated into identifiable discount and other incentive components, or does its economic substance require a single classification?","Which evidence establishes gift status and discount status for each component?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED] For the selected paragraph 3.11 gift control, true means the assessed distributor offers this component to a client in a qualifying product or product-type promotion, the component is a gift, and it is not a discount of fees or charges. False means this component does not meet that selected restriction predicate; it does not establish overall compliance or exempt other components. Unknown classifications remain unknown. Apply the predicate separately to each component of a combined offer.","subject":"Paragraph 3.11 gift restriction applied to an individual benefit component"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.97af37a2579f59b0ee43211f","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"fd1353007afb88c6117d9461019ca0bb0eff6dfc020965979cd65f2c62c6ed1f","candidate_id":"candidate.16b604d3418541b593500f1b681b8445","commitment":"6d6e7adc6faa9d94b74c08e597df4fe7feceed690e1cf22bbb3616324b9e9e70","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.6d6e7adc6faa9d94b74c08e5","order":2,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["The selected control assesses one identified benefit offered by one distributor in the SFC-authorised-fund context.","Separately identifiable benefits in a combined offer are assessed separately; identifying those benefits may require judgment.","Gift classification, discount classification and promotional linkage are supplied judgments, not inferred from a benefit’s label or from the mere existence of additional returns.","The result is interpreted only when scope is true; unknown facts remain unknown."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u0.2"},{"quote":"(i) the actual return of the relevant fund(s) invested by the investor (ie, fund return); and (ii) a top-up return to make up the difference between the fund return and the guaranteed rate of return offered by the distributor.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u7.1360"},{"quote":"Even where the guaranteed returns offered would not constitute a “structured product” under the SFO","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u14.3675"}],"distinction":"The discount exception applies to the identified benefit, while product-type promotion remains covered. For example, an offer promoting funds of one fund house could combine a fee reduction with a separately identifiable shopping voucher. Assuming the voucher is a gift and not a fee discount, the fee reduction satisfies this control and the voucher fails it. The text does not support exempting the entire package because one component is a discount, or excluding it because no individual fund is singled out. A fee-linked cash rebate presents a genuine unresolved classification question: if it is a discount it satisfies this control; if it is a non-discount gift it fails. The packet does not supply enough criteria to choose between those classifications.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The offeror is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds in the transaction being assessed.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit is offered to a client in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product, including a relevant fund type or funds offered by a particular fund house.","name":"benefit_has_product_promotion_link","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit qualifies as a gift under the referenced paragraph 3.11 standard; being an additional return or incentive alone does not establish this fact.","name":"benefit_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit itself qualifies as a discount of fees or charges, rather than merely accompanying a separate discount.","name":"benefit_is_fee_or_charge_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(or (not benefit_is_gift) benefit_is_fee_or_charge_discount)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor benefit_has_product_promotion_link)"},"local_id":"gift_component_control","questions":["Does the identified benefit qualify as a gift, and if so does it itself constitute a discount of fees or charges?","Does the referenced FAQ clarify treatment of rebates or inseparable combined benefits?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] For the selected control, Paragraph 3.11 gift restriction for one offered benefit, true means that the in-scope benefit is either not a gift or qualifies for the fee-or-charge discount exception. False means that it is an in-scope gift outside that exception and fails the stated should-not-offer standard. This is a proposed interpretation of that control only; it does not determine compliance of other offer components, section 103 compliance or whole-firm compliance.","subject":"A separately identified benefit offered by a distributor during promotion to a client"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.6d6e7adc6faa9d94b74c08e5","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"586262f99ee83fde1c3e2ce14d1c1cdaae0c433909759b87f05d0fa36db9435a","candidate_id":"candidate.c645662376e842e98ef3e254bfe1fc93","commitment":"142f34016b300f5c110eb249951b9b557d69bbee80a2fc841feda9ed7dbcbc3b","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.142f34016b300f5c110eb249","order":3,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["The assessed provider is treated as a distributor only after its role in distributing the relevant funds has been established.","Gift status requires a substantive classification of the particular benefit. The statement that guaranteed returns or other incentives may be considered gifts does not make every such return or incentive a gift automatically.","Fee-or-charge-discount status applies to the substance of the assessed component, not merely to the label used for the combined offer.","Separately identifiable benefits are assessed separately. Where an arrangement cannot reliably be decomposed, component boundaries require judgment before this model can be applied.","The particular-product-type relationship includes the source's examples of certain types of funds and funds offered by certain fund houses.","The result concerns only the quoted paragraph 3.11 gift restriction and confers no legal approval."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors) have been offering additional returns or other incentives that may divert the client’s focus from properly considering the risks and features of the underlying funds.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u0.2"},{"quote":"Typically, the “guaranteed returns” in such cases comprise: (i) the actual return of the relevant fund(s) invested by the investor (ie, fund return); and (ii) a top-up return to make up the difference between the fund return and the guaranteed rate of return offered by the distributor.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u7.1360"},{"quote":"Even where the guaranteed returns offered would not constitute a “structured product” under the SFO, distributors are reminded to have regard to paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct in offering such returns or other incentives in promoting SFC-authorised funds, as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"quote":"Paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct provides that distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement as investors may be distracted from the unique features and risks of such particular funds3.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"}],"distinction":"A single offer-level Boolean such as 'contains a discount' would hide separate benefits and could incorrectly extend the discount exception to an accompanying gift. A Boolean limited to promotion of a named fund would also miss promotion of a fund type or funds from a particular fund house. Finally, 'guaranteed return' cannot stand in for 'gift': the source distinguishes fund return from distributor top-up and uses qualified gift-classification language.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The provider of the assessed component acts as an intermediary distributing the relevant funds in this promotional context. Establishing this regulatory role requires professional judgment.","name":"provider_is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean for the assessed provider and promotional context"},{"meaning":"The provider offers this particular benefit component to the assessed client at the assessment time; actual payment or receipt is not required. Supply from the offer evidence.","name":"component_offered_to_client","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean for one component, provider, client and offer time"},{"meaning":"Offering the assessed component forms part of promoting an identified specific investment product to the client. Classifying the promotional connection requires professional judgment.","name":"component_promotes_specific_product","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean promotional relationship for the assessed component"},{"meaning":"Offering the assessed component is linked to promoting a particular type of investment product to the client, including certain fund types or funds offered by certain fund houses. Classifying the type and connection requires professional judgment.","name":"component_promotes_particular_product_type","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean promotional relationship for the assessed component"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit component is substantively classified as a gift for the quoted restriction. A guaranteed return or other incentive requires individual assessment rather than automatic classification; fund return and distributor top-up must be distinguished where relevant. Supplying this classification requires professional judgment.","name":"component_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u7.1360","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean classification of one benefit component"},{"meaning":"The assessed component itself reduces fees or charges and is substantively a discount of those fees or charges. A separate discount elsewhere in the offer does not make this fact true. Supplying this classification requires professional judgment.","name":"component_is_fee_or_charge_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean classification of one benefit component"}],"result":"(and component_offered_to_client (or component_promotes_specific_product component_promotes_particular_product_type) component_is_gift (not component_is_fee_or_charge_discount))","result_type":"bool","scope":"provider_is_distributor"},"local_id":"component_gift_prohibition","questions":["Who provides each benefit, and is that provider acting as the distributor in the assessed promotion?","What distinct benefits does the offer contain, and which amounts arise from the underlying fund rather than an additional distributor undertaking?","On what substantive basis should each component be classified as a gift?","Does each claimed discount actually reduce identified fees or charges, and can it be separated from other promised benefits?","What promotional terms link each component to a specific product or a particular product type, including any link through a fund house?","When was the component offered, and what offer terms and product documents applied then?","Does further guidance, including the referenced FAQ whose answer is not supplied, affect the classification of the particular arrangement?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED] For an assessed distributor within scope, the result answers whether offering this particular benefit component to the client falls within the quoted gift restriction: the component is offered in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product, is classified as a gift, and is not a discount of fees or charges. True means that this component's offer falls within that restriction. False means that the conjunction is not met for this component; it does not establish that the combined offer is compliant or legally approved. Unknown inputs remain unknown unless the expression can be determined from the other inputs.","subject":"Application of the gift restriction to one component of a product or product-type promotion"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.142f34016b300f5c110eb249","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"c110b7c8b6506e151958dd008461e5225ee74e977445e7ae3cf59f7fafa3aeae","candidate_id":"candidate.8fede9ef89084ceba11540db0199e293","commitment":"2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564ee1ce2958e3880b515982b5a31babe53b9b4ca7ef","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e","order":4,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["Economically distinct benefits in a combined offer can be identified separately; this is an interpretive modeling choice for applying 'any gifts' and the fee/charge discount exception.","A component is classified as a gift only after examining its terms and economic substance. Paragraph 9's 'may be considered a gift' does not establish that every additional return or incentive is a gift.","The fee/charge discount exception applies to the component that is itself such a discount, rather than to all benefits packaged with it.","The phrase 'should not offer' is represented as a prohibition under this selected Code of Conduct restriction; the result does not determine criminal liability or compliance with other requirements."],"citations":[{"quote":"Paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct provides that distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement as investors may be distracted from the unique features and risks of such particular funds3.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"Even where the guaranteed returns offered would not constitute a “structured product” under the SFO, distributors are reminded to have regard to paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct in offering such returns or other incentives in promoting SFC-authorised funds, as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"quote":"Typically, the “guaranteed returns” in such cases comprise: (i) the actual return of the relevant fund(s) invested by the investor (ie, fund return); and (ii) a top-up return to make up the difference between the fund return and the guaranteed rate of return offered by the distributor.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u7.1360"}],"distinction":"A single offer-level Boolean such as 'includes a discount' would hide the difference between an excepted fee discount and a separate potentially prohibited gift. A Boolean limited to promotion of a named fund would also omit product-type promotion, including funds from particular fund houses. Finally, absence of structured-product classification does not remove the need to classify the component under the gift restriction.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The actor making the assessed offer acts as a distributor within the quoted restriction.","name":"offeror_is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean classification of the offeror for this offer"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit component is offered by that actor to the identified client at the assessment time; receipt or payment is not required by this fact.","name":"component_offered_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean occurrence for one component, client and offer time"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit component falls within 'gifts' in the quoted restriction, assessed separately from whether it qualifies for the discount exception. Being an additional return or incentive alone does not fix this fact as true.","name":"component_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean substantive classification of one benefit component"},{"meaning":"The assessed component itself constitutes a discount of identifiable fees or charges. A separate discount elsewhere in the offer does not make this fact true.","name":"component_is_fee_or_charge_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean exception classification of one benefit component"},{"meaning":"The assessed component is offered in promoting a specific investment product to the client.","name":"component_promotes_specific_product","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean promotional relation for this component and offer"},{"meaning":"The assessed component is offered in promoting, or in a manner linked to, a particular type of investment product, including a specified type of fund or funds offered by specified fund houses.","name":"component_linked_to_product_type","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean promotional relation for this component and offer"}],"result":"(and component_is_gift (not component_is_fee_or_charge_discount) (or component_promotes_specific_product component_linked_to_product_type))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and offeror_is_distributor component_offered_to_client)"},"local_id":"component_gift_prohibition","questions":["Who makes the offer, to whom is it made, and in what distributor capacity?","What are the offer's distinct benefit components, terms and presentation at the time of offering?","For each component, what supports classification as a gift, and does it actually reduce identifiable fees or charges?","Does the component promote a specific investment product or connect to a particular product type, including funds from specified fund houses?","Does the referenced FAQ supply qualifications affecting component separation, gift classification or the discount exception?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED] Within scope, the result answers whether offering this component is prohibited by the selected gift restriction: true means the component is a gift, is not a discount of fees or charges, and promotes a specific investment product or is linked to a particular type of investment product. False means this component does not meet that conjunction; it does not establish that the combined offer is compliant or legally approved. An unknown classification or promotional connection remains unknown unless the other facts logically determine the result.","subject":"Application of the paragraph 10 gift restriction to an individual component of a promotional offer"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"801b24549fa0e9c033373a4ab755488af02666c6a11f6b666c01ac2aefa244e8","candidate_id":"candidate.ef9617c1b03543be9082d8450c6ebabf","commitment":"bc55be7e973a689d07f9e64b2bf944b389ae1a54dec39996adaee92863ee159e","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.bc55be7e973a689d07f9e64b","order":5,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["The restriction attaches to a distributor's act of offering a gift. The quoted text does not additionally require the distributor to fund or fulfil it.","Separately identifiable benefit components are assessed separately; boundaries require judgment where benefits cannot reliably be separated.","Gift status requires substantive assessment. Guaranteed returns and other incentives are not automatically gifts merely because paragraph 9 says they may be considered gifts.","The fee or charge discount exception applies to the assessed component itself, not every benefit packaged with a discount.","Product-type promotion includes funds identified by fund type or fund house.","The words 'should not offer' are modeled as a prohibition under this selected restriction, without determining criminal liability or granting legal approval."],"citations":[{"quote":"Paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct provides that distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement as investors may be distracted from the unique features and risks of such particular funds3.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"Even where the guaranteed returns offered would not constitute a “structured product” under the SFO, distributors are reminded to have regard to paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct in offering such returns or other incentives in promoting SFC-authorised funds, as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"quote":"Typically, the “guaranteed returns” in such cases comprise: (i) the actual return of the relevant fund(s) invested by the investor (ie, fund return); and (ii) a top-up return to make up the difference between the fund return and the guaranteed rate of return offered by the distributor.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u7.1360"}],"distinction":"The prior component model abstraction.ea48395ee1fc075eb75b04b4 describes the distributor as the provider and places provider_is_distributor in scope. If 'provider' means the funder or fulfiller, that vocabulary can exclude a gift offered by a distributor but supplied by another person. This proposal separates offering from funding and fulfilment. It is a consequential correction to that possible narrowing, while remaining compatible with abstraction.933486dc69f18e0075717cc1's offeror-based scope. Neither third-party funding nor any actual third-party arrangement is assumed.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The actor making the assessed offer acts as a distributor in this promotional context, independently of who funds or fulfils the benefit.","name":"offeror_is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean classification of the offeror"},{"meaning":"The assessed actor offers this benefit component to the identified client at the assessment time. Attribution of the offer must be established; funding, fulfilment, acceptance and payment are not prerequisites for this fact.","name":"actor_offers_component_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean offering relation for one actor, component, client and time"},{"meaning":"The assessed component is substantively classified as a gift under the quoted restriction, separately from the discount exception. Its being a guaranteed return or incentive alone does not establish this classification.","name":"component_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u7.1360","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean classification of one benefit component"},{"meaning":"The assessed component itself constitutes a discount of identifiable fees or charges. A discount in another component does not satisfy this fact.","name":"component_is_fee_or_charge_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean exception classification of one benefit component"},{"meaning":"Offering this component promotes an identified specific investment product to the client.","name":"component_promotes_specific_product","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean promotional relation"},{"meaning":"Offering this component is linked to promoting a particular type of investment product, including certain fund types or funds offered by certain fund houses.","name":"component_promotes_product_type","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean promotional relation"}],"result":"(and actor_offers_component_to_client component_is_gift (not component_is_fee_or_charge_discount) (or component_promotes_specific_product component_promotes_product_type))","result_type":"bool","scope":"offeror_is_distributor"},"local_id":"offering_distinct_from_fulfilment","questions":["Who makes the offer to the client, and in what distributor capacity?","Who funds or fulfils each benefit, and does the evidence establish that the distributor offers it rather than merely describing an independently available benefit?","What are the distinct benefit components and their terms at the time of offering?","What supports gift classification and any claimed reduction of identifiable fees or charges for each component?","How is the component linked to a specific investment product or a particular product type?","Does the referenced FAQ qualify attribution of an offer, component boundaries, gift status or the discount exception?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED] Within distributor scope, the result answers whether this actor's offering of this component to this client falls within the selected gift prohibition. True means the actor offers a gift that is not itself a fee or charge discount and has the specified product or product-type promotional connection, irrespective of who funds or fulfils it. False means that conjunction is not met for this component; it does not approve the combined offer. Unknown facts remain unknown unless other inputs determine the expression.","subject":"Attribution of the gift offer separately from funding or fulfilment"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.bc55be7e973a689d07f9e64b","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"6e66a0b1a71922890fa254fe76891fd1aaa191ca3231ee30430861e638455fc1","candidate_id":"candidate.9d79b627dee94ae892236f4e815a7191","commitment":"bca408c75cbf8467afafada69a45780a2ff6e2dfdeaf541dfac90127c2ec9128","depth":1,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.bca408c75cbf8467afafada6","order":6,"parent":"node.968dbccb08282a4e8a580ae5","reading":{"assumptions":["The selected offer has a finite, separately identifiable component inventory.","Unknown classifications remain unknown.","This is an interpretation proposal, not a legal determination."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u0.2"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"}],"distinction":"The exception is component-specific: a fee or charge discount is excluded from the gift prohibition, while a distinct non-discount gift remains caught. Product-type promotion is expressly included. A guaranteed return is not automatically a gift; classification is required.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The selected actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds.","name":"actor_is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The offer promotes a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","name":"promotion_scope_satisfied","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"At least one separately identifiable offered component is a gift and is not a discount of fees or charges.","name":"non_discount_gift_component","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(and actor_is_distributor promotion_scope_satisfied non_discount_gift_component)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and actor_is_distributor promotion_scope_satisfied)"},"local_id":"component_specific_exception","questions":["How should an inseparable combined benefit be classified?","What evidence establishes that a benefit is a fee or charge discount rather than another incentive?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED] True means the selected distributor offer is within the client/product-or-type scope and contains a non-discount gift component caught by the quoted should-not-offer rule. False means at least one required condition is established absent; it does not establish whole-firm compliance or resolve section 103.","subject":"Paragraph 3.11 gift restriction for one promotional offer"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.968dbccb08282a4e8a580ae5","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":null,"candidate_id":"candidate.fc8249a22d524f6586f5fdc2b61f7eb1","commitment":"6acbec2ab4ab87e82291b9ffe6425f4c23fc1cb18ae95105e31ea9f564f8f816","depth":1,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":{"code":"E_UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE","details":"None"},"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.6acbec2ab4ab87e82291b9ff","order":7,"parent":"node.968dbccb08282a4e8a580ae5","reading":{"assumptions":["The offer is assessed as one indivisible package.","The package is treated according to its dominant or principal economic character, if such a character can be established."],"citations":[{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges)","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"}],"distinction":"A competing reading treats the exception as applying to the combined package when its principal character is a fee or charge discount. The supplied text does not provide a dominance or inseparability test, so this reading is materially less supported and cannot be operationalised without additional authority.","family":"exceptions","formalization":null,"local_id":"package_level_exception","questions":["Does the referenced FAQ or full Code specify how bundled or inseparable benefits are classified?","Can the package be decomposed economically and contractually?"],"statement":"The source leaves unresolved whether a genuinely inseparable package containing a discount and another benefit is assessed component-by-component or as a whole package.","subject":"Alternative attachment of the fee/charge discount exception"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.968dbccb08282a4e8a580ae5","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0}],"pending":null,"provider_id":"codex.fresh.v1.compact.v1","retrievals":[{"missing_dependencies":[],"node_id":"node.968dbccb08282a4e8a580ae5","retained_uncited_units":[{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 497:507","normative":true,"span":{"end":507,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u1.497","page":1,"quote_sha256":"ea2b8a878841df5955c78edc6cae47446483b86e3f5ccb04e1a8d940cf7e59fd","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":497,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Background","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u1.497"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 512:787","normative":true,"span":{"end":787,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u2.512","page":1,"quote_sha256":"1af11939ea26428b3ebc908947bc9c1f16f0e153b769d724370e402bef46d880","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":512,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"In some cases, distributors promoted SFC-authorised funds (often via online platforms) and offered or imposed additional or distinct features or restrictions (eg, “guaranteed returns” or “lock-up periods”) beyond the product features set out in the funds’ offering documents.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u2.512"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 792:1110","normative":true,"span":{"end":1110,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u3.792","page":1,"quote_sha256":"bb5d6d0066f0f3d1f31abecdaf338ffa59419754230c95ee338e84e9f9bf3161","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":792,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"In other cases, distributors asked clients to provide a mandate or standing instruction to invest in one or more SFC-authorised funds under specific circumstances, eg, using idle money in a client’s securities trading account with an aim to generate additional returns, albeit without any guaranteed or specific rates.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u3.792"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 1115:1265","normative":true,"span":{"end":1265,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u4.1115","page":1,"quote_sha256":"8f21351a0ccdff701f2cc91871495aa1a1f6c2eb489975ea56821f8b71361cda","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":1115,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"These SFC-authorised funds and services were often promoted by the distributors to the public through aggressive and high-profile marketing campaigns.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u4.1115"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 1267:1285","normative":true,"span":{"end":1285,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u5.1267","page":1,"quote_sha256":"3502a56f7cfc1882bcea56240e2049ac086a6dd493f2f798572984a462255832","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":1267,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Guaranteed returns","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u5.1267"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 1287:1355","normative":true,"span":{"end":1355,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u6.1287","page":1,"quote_sha256":"03c2ce4fec643340916926d6501ab8c112939a4757a21957ef88cb03e5d60fdb","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":1287,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Section 103 of the Securities and Futures Ordinance (Cap. 571) (SFO)","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u6.1287"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 1360:1646","normative":true,"span":{"end":1646,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u7.1360","page":1,"quote_sha256":"94608f831bfe0bc9746af9dc0219689b16aafe90a74711539afe5f3d6f65302e","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":1360,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Typically, the “guaranteed returns” in such cases comprise: (i) the actual return of the relevant fund(s) invested by the investor (ie, fund return); and (ii) a top-up return to make up the difference between the fund return and the guaranteed rate of return offered by the distributor.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u7.1360"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 1651:1935","normative":true,"span":{"end":1935,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u8.1651","page":1,"quote_sha256":"c775d212de8b31011848e316ed775c7903d2a3439d14f1d0b43c68812f8f7fc6","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":1651,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"The SFC wishes to remind intermediaries who engage in promotional activities that these guaranteed return arrangements may constitute a \"structured product\" under the SFO if the return to investors is determined by reference to the change in value of any securities (including funds).","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u8.1651"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 1940:2234","normative":true,"span":{"end":2234,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u9.1940","page":1,"quote_sha256":"da3d5056c84f1786f1d7407d2638edfe2d9c59c7c2bfab11e30f99901b252a22","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":1940,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"It is an offence under section 103 of the SFO for a person to issue an advertisement, invitation or document which is or contains an invitation to the Hong Kong public to enter into or offer to enter into any structured products, unless the SFC has authorised the issue or an exemption applies.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u9.1940"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 2239:2601","normative":true,"span":{"end":2601,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u10.2239","page":1,"quote_sha256":"b226a3d2cbdb1fed01e7c813e12644c991178112e7df12c5b5b06ada5cd3ff7e","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":2239,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"SFC-authorised funds without guaranteed features are required to highlight in their offering documents that they do not have these features and that investors may not get back the principal of their investment1. As such, any guaranteed returns provided by distributors may create a misleading impression that these returns are provided by the underlying fund(s).","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u10.2239"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 2603:2641","normative":true,"span":{"end":2641,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u11.2603","page":1,"quote_sha256":"195534ad5daed52e7ac87063b4aecc79dc0bb389cebc88cc9215bac090ef2f22","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":2603,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct2","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u11.2603"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 4022:4058","normative":true,"span":{"end":4058,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u15.4022","page":1,"quote_sha256":"dda918bbe82f30ddab28135039fbc339acf16acc07deb67f6babf9b2b2757743","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":4022,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Lock-up period and dealing frequency","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u15.4022"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 4063:4354","normative":true,"span":{"end":4354,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u16.4063","page":1,"quote_sha256":"2f891b58037e676dcd695c3baf69a86f4853ed05e667c205c42107b8af4b853f","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":4063,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"When distributing SFC-authorised funds, some distributors imposed a lock-up period on their clients’ investments or lowered the funds’ dealing frequency. For instance, clients’ redemption was only allowed on a weekly or monthly basis even though the fund provided daily dealing arrangements.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u16.4063"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 4359:4874","normative":true,"span":{"end":4874,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u17.4359","page":1,"quote_sha256":"08297ac978b8b5eaf5dfc9048caf8c3b306c0cb224d151e2108633ea28bb7597","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":4359,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Distributors should act fairly and in the best interests of their clients in providing services in accordance with General Principle 1 (Honesty and fairness) of the Code of Conduct. They should not restrict a client’s right to redeem his or her investment in a fund pursuant to the dealing frequency specified in the fund’s offering documents. Such restrictions would limit the client’s ability to make effective and timely investment decisions in response to changing market conditions or individual circumstances.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u17.4359"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 4879:5228","normative":true,"span":{"end":5228,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u18.4879","page":1,"quote_sha256":"3d8087781b49ce535e15631e7265887d0afb4fbe07c78026ba6deb62cf847c20","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":4879,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"While distributors of SFC-authorised funds may have different fund dealing procedures or cut-off times for administrative efficiency, the SFC expects them to use their best endeavours to adhere to a fund’s dealing frequency as stipulated in its offering documents when dealing in the fund for clients, and not to reduce the fund’s dealing frequency.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u18.4879"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 5230:5252","normative":true,"span":{"end":5252,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u19.5230","page":1,"quote_sha256":"7e1dfa66af384d4b087a94fecfb2cecfa563dd744d656ea862ae5f640932f566","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":5230,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Other marketing issues","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u19.5230"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 5257:5898","normative":true,"span":{"end":5898,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u20.5257","page":1,"quote_sha256":"994420732f7ffb764258e7b4c4c102643e363748d0214053741f033cbfb141eb","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":5257,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"In some cases, distributors offered or marketed the services described in paragraph 3 above without any guaranteed rates of return, but highlighted the regular interest payments or distribution features of the services prominently (eg, interest generated daily, or clients’ potential financial return from using such services), which would in fact be derived from the actual return(s) of the underlying fund(s). In preparing invitations and advertisements to promote their services, intermediaries should ensure that they do not contain any misleading or deceptive information, and they must comply with paragraph 2.3 of the Code of Conduct.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u20.5257"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 5903:6369","normative":true,"span":{"end":6369,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u21.5903","page":1,"quote_sha256":"bc704754c5b7c9c59e6a6b494dd6f9505f930ae4b36a37aa02d6368c69a4edf2","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":5903,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Where a distributor highlights in an advertisement the financial return of its services, which is in fact derived from the actual return(s) of the underlying SFC-authorised fund(s), the advertisement, particularly the presentation of financial return relating to the services, should be prepared in a manner that is consistent with the principles under the SFC’s Advertising Guidelines Applicable to Collective Investment Schemes Authorized under the Product Codes4.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u21.5903"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 6374:7002","normative":true,"span":{"end":7002,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u22.6374","page":1,"quote_sha256":"20ecbac168ce1f7902c8b60784189a57017881fb8408fea1d9d3bd707bea3b74","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":6374,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Specifically, the advertisements of these services should avoid giving a misleading impression that the relevant services or underlying fund(s) would generate positive or guaranteed returns without any risk of loss. In addition, the advertisements should not draw a parallel between the services and the placement of cash on deposits, imply they are deposit-like arrangements (including any comparisons between the financial returns of the services and bank deposit rates), or suggest that the services are, or are equivalent to, bank deposits or savings (eg, by emphasising the services can address investors’ “savings needs”).","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u22.6374"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 7007:7178","normative":true,"span":{"end":7178,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u23.7007","page":1,"quote_sha256":"b9db4855c8d4944ebdfe0009a08ee4d1623c21e673c1c221a04b1bab3f6497ec","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":7007,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"The SFC will closely monitor market practices concerning the promotion of SFC-authorised funds and may take regulatory action and issue further guidance where appropriate.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u23.7007"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 7186:7274","normative":true,"span":{"end":7274,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u24.7186","page":1,"quote_sha256":"0e3225addfcc2663ed547268443c0eda4c4b22cc50e1f858008119256b3a532c","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":7186,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Intermediaries Supervision Department                       Investment Products Division","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u24.7186"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 7275:7392","normative":true,"span":{"end":7392,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u25.7275","page":1,"quote_sha256":"65ef453c883837716ab8837d02d9559715cd243baf93ca1a5cf70be2d67b8492","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":7275,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Intermediaries Division                                                             Securities and Futures Commission","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u25.7275"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 7393:7426","normative":true,"span":{"end":7426,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u26.7393","page":1,"quote_sha256":"88e2bc94e9edc39f2ac1cdaaea86b44ab5ea59b31c446f69591f21bf460b005e","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":7393,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Securities and Futures Commission","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u26.7393"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 7511:7985","normative":true,"span":{"end":7985,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u27.7511","page":1,"quote_sha256":"bf5f8b77f3976a352737ec8fbcfd51cec4ddf8c7ebfa8bcec39b200cf36f6a6c","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":7511,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"1 Pursuant to 6.4 of the Overarching Principles Section as set out in the SFC Handbook for Unit Trusts and Mutual Funds, Investment-Linked Assurance Schemes and Unlisted Structured Investment Products, offering documents of an SFC-authorised fund shall contain the information necessary for investors to be able to make an informed judgement of the investment whilst all key features and risks of the fund shall be highlighted prominently in a succinct manner for investors.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u27.7511"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 7987:8108","normative":true,"span":{"end":8108,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u28.7987","page":1,"quote_sha256":"4c6f6c26a269f1395844e4e68ad8b7b0dc9a752bf58521543258b9ca6360144b","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","start":7987,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"2 The Code of Conduct for Persons Licensed by or Registered with the Securities and Futures Commission (Code of Conduct).","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u28.7987"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=23EC46 chars 8110:8233","normative":true,"span":{"end":8233,"id":"s.db43e253bea18.u29.8110","page":1,"quote_sha256":"7d1b57b24a3d3a602b7413d75e6e6c8469cf4f2366245996989f8837b9944ce3","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"db43e253bea18","star